    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "During the past seven years, I visited a few countries that were in need of clean water. And I met some of the most "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "inspiring",
            "ref": "v-inspiring"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " people I’ve ever known."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "By the time I reached my first village in "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Mozambique",
            "zh": "莫桑比克"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", a small crowd had already gathered around the water point to meet me. These people were "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "eager",
            "ref": "v-eager"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to talk about the difference clean water had made in their community."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "At the front of the crowd, I met Natalia, a 15-year-old girl. Access to clean water had enabled her to have better health. She could spend more time in school. As a result, she had become better educated than many of her fellow villagers."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I asked Natalia’s mother what she expected of her daughter’s future. “My dream is for Natalia to become a teacher,” she said proudly. Natalia happened to "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "overhear",
            "zh": "无意中听到"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " our conversation. And she turned around to say, “I don’t want to be just a teacher. I want to be the headteacher.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Many people I met in Mozambique told me that water is life. Having access to clean water would immediately improve health. Healthier families would save money on hospital bills. Healthier kids would spend more time in school. Like Natalia, they would have bigger dreams as well as better opportunities."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Yet 748 million people on this planet don’t have access to clean water. Every morning, they stand in line in front of a muddy hole in the ground. They carry dirty water all the way home and serve it to the people they love most. They "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "constantly",
            "ref": "v-constantly"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " suffer from stomach pains."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "You and I just got lucky to be born in places where we’ve never had to worry about finding clean water."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
